# deploy-checklist

Mark each item ✅ done / ❌ blocked / ⏭ n/a. Deploys happen through the pipeline after a merge to
`{{ project.default_branch }}`. Nobody applies infrastructure or manifests by hand.

## Reference values
| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Cloud / region | {{ infra.cloud }} / `{{ infra.region }}` |
| Cluster | `{{#if infra.cluster}}{{ infra.cluster }}{{else}}<CLUSTER>{{/if}}` |
| Image repository | `{{#if infra.registry}}{{ infra.registry }}{{else}}<REGISTRY>/<IMAGE>{{/if}}` |
| App / namespace | `{{ infra.app_name }}` / `{{ infra.namespace }}` |
| Health endpoint | `{{ infra.health_path }}` (port {{ infra.app_port }}) |
| Deploy environment | GitHub environment `{{ infra.environment }}` |

Keep real account IDs, domains and contact emails **out of this file**: it lives in git.

## Pre-deploy
- [ ] All CI checks green on the PR; the merge gate allowed the merge
- [ ] Image tagged with the git SHA, never `:latest`
- [ ] Terraform plan read in the plan job's run summary **before** approving the apply: no
      unexpected destroys or replacements (apply refuses to run if the plan changed since)
- [ ] Manifest changes reviewed in the PR diff
- [ ] New secrets created where the app reads them{{#if infra.vault}} (Vault){{/if}} **before** the deploy
- [ ] New settings have safe defaults, so the app starts without them
- [ ] A reviewer approved the `{{ infra.environment }}` environment deployment in GitHub Actions

## During deploy (watch it, don't walk away)
- [ ] Terraform: plan published, apply approved, apply matched the reviewed plan
- [ ] Platform stage: every release upgrades cleanly
- [ ] Build: image scan passes (no CRITICAL/HIGH)
- [ ] Deploy: {{#if infra.argocd}}ArgoCD reports the app Synced and Healthy{{else}}rollout completes{{/if}}

If the rollout fails, read the previous container's logs first:
```bash
kubectl logs -n {{ infra.namespace }} deployment/{{ infra.app_name }} --previous
```

## Smoke tests (after the pipeline finishes)
- [ ] `curl -fsS https://<APP_HOST>{{ infra.health_path }}` returns healthy
- [ ] Sign-in works end to end with a test account
- [ ] The main user journey works; degraded modes (e.g. a missing optional API key) are expected, broken pages are not
- [ ] Error rate and latency dashboards look normal for 15 minutes

## Rollback
**Option A: roll back the workload (fastest)**
```bash
{{#if infra.argocd}}# ArgoCD would re-sync the bad tag: revert the tag commit in git instead (option B),
# or pause auto-sync first if you must act on the cluster.
{{/if}}kubectl rollout undo deployment/{{ infra.app_name }} -n {{ infra.namespace }}
kubectl rollout status deployment/{{ infra.app_name }} -n {{ infra.namespace }}
```
**Option B: revert in git (the pipeline redeploys the previous version)**
```bash
git switch -c fix/revert-<slug> && git revert <bad-merge-commit> && git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --fill   # merges like any PR: green checks, then the pipeline redeploys
```
Afterwards: write down what was deployed, what failed and how it was rolled back (issue or incident note).
